(`Free` through one of two buffer parameters naming one buffer empties it
 under both names, and the caller's.)
To 'merge' of a buffer called first and a buffer called second.
    Free first.
    Print "second sees: {second's size}".
    append "after" to second.
    On error print "the append was refused".
    Print "second now: {second}".

a buffer called hold is "ab".
'merge' of hold and hold.
Print "hold: {hold}".
